# Branding: an ORDERED search path (`:`-separated, like $PATH) of roots under which brand archives
# (`*.tar.gz`) are found recursively. An earlier root SHADOWS a later one for the brand ids it
# provides — nothing is ever deleted to settle that. Build each brand's `dist/<id>.tar.gz` with
# `node packages/branding/scripts/build-dev-brandings.ts`, then point this at the deployment configs.
# The active brand is switched live in the admin Branding tab; pin one for dev with
# OCELOT_ACTIVE_BRANDING. Iterate on a single brand without a rebuild:
#   node packages/branding/scripts/build-brand-archive.ts <brand-dir> <brand-dir>/dist/<id>.tar.gz --watch
# then edit brand.config.ts and refresh the browser. Leave unset for vanilla.
#
# OCELOT_BRANDING_CACHE_DIR is the one directory the webapp WRITES: server-middleware/branding-sync.js
# mirrors the backend's archives there and owns it exclusively (it overwrites and removes files). Keep
# it out of the config tree — pointing it at deployment/configurations would have the sync compete with
# your own brand builds. Listing it LAST below is what makes a locally built brand beat the backend's
# copy, so `--watch` shows your edits; swap the order to test what the backend actually serves.
# Defaults to the first root of the search path when unset.
# OCELOT_BRANDING_ASSETS_DIR=../deployment/configurations:.branding-cache
# OCELOT_BRANDING_CACHE_DIR=.branding-cache
# OCELOT_ACTIVE_BRANDING=
